{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_64","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Register memory lane sideband\n=============================\n\nWhat changed:\n- Added EX/MEM sideband fields for replicated memory write data, byte-lane mask, and memory misalignment.\n- Moved byte/half/word store-data replication, mask generation, and load/store misalignment detection from MEM into EX before the EX/MEM latch.\n- Updated MEM to drive dmem write data, write enables, read enable, RVFI masks, RVFI write data, and trap gating from the registered sideband.\n- Updated the top-level forwarding misalignment kill to use the registered EX/MEM sideband.\n- Added pipeline tests for LB/LBU/LH/LHU/LW masks and load extension, SB/SH/SW replicated data and masks, and misaligned load/store trapping with no masks.\n\nDeviations:\n- Removed the old EX/MEM raw store-data field instead of keeping it alongside the new replicated sideband. The same post-forward rs2 value is already carried as rs2_val for RVFI, so the old field was redundant.\n\nConcerns:\n- The MEM-stage load-data extraction still uses the registered effective address low bits directly, as intended. No new pipeline stage was added.\n- Plain `make cosim TARGET=bench` failed before simulation because `test/cosim/build.sh` defaults to `NRET=2` while this core declares `nret: 1`. Rerunning with `NRET=1` matches core.yaml and passes.\n- Timing was not run locally.\n\nLocal status:\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- Formal: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed using `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`.\n- Cocotb unit tests: pass, `python3 -m pytest cores/bench/test`.\n- Cosim: pass with `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
