{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_78","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"One-hot fast ALU selects\n\nChanged the ID/EX control bundle from a compact 5-bit ALU operation field to\na 19-bit one-hot vector. The decoder still exposes the legacy 5-bit alu_op\noutput for the standalone decoder unit tests, but the pipeline latches and\nuses only the one-hot alu_oh vector.\n\nUpdated alu.sv to gate precomputed result groups with one-hot enables instead\nof selecting through a binary case tree. The ALTOPS substitutions are preserved\nfor MUL/DIV/REM-class ops, and real DIV/REM outputs remain zero in the\ncombinational ALU because ex_stage still routes those through div_unit.\n\nUpdated ex_stage.sv and div_unit.sv so DIV/REM detection, divider signed/rem\nmode selection, and ALU instantiation consume the one-hot vector directly.\nForwarding, branch redirect, memory stall behavior, divider handoff, and\npipeline register timing are unchanged.\n\nDeviations: kept decoder.alu_op as a compatibility/test output instead of\nremoving it outright. It is not carried in ctrl_t or used by EX.\n\nConcerns: the one-hot output mux is written as gated ORs. This removes the\n5-bit op comparisons from EX, but final QoR depends on how Gowin packs the\ngating and OR tree versus the prior case mux.\n\nLocal checks:\n- Verilator lint: pass\n- Formal: pass, RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh\n  reported 53 passed, 0 failed\n- Cosim: pass with NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench. A first plain\n  make cosim TARGET=bench build used the script default NRET=2 and failed\n  before simulation because this core correctly exposes only nret=1 RVFI ports.\n- Cocotb unit tests: pass, make test TARGET=bench\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
