{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'nl -ba cores/bench/rtl/core.sv'", "aggregated_output": "     1\t// rtl/core.sv\n     2\t//\n     3\t// Top-level wiring for the 5-stage in-order RV32IM core.\n     4\t//\n     5\t//  IF -> ID -> EX -> MEM -> WB\n     6\t//   |    |     ^\n     7\t//   |    +-----+    forward_unit drives EX-stage rs1/rs2 muxes\n     8\t//   |               from EX/MEM and MEM/WB\n     9\t//   +- stall <- hazard_unit (load-use)\n    10\t//\n    11\t// IO port names use the `io_*` Chisel-emit prefix so the existing\n    12\t// formal/wrapper_si.sv and test/cosim/main.cpp bindings carry through\n    13\t// byte-for-byte. RVFI port set is the single-channel set described in\n    14\t// CLAUDE.md invariant 1 under `nret: 1` (declared in core.yaml). The\n    15\t// orchestrator routes formal to wrapper_si.sv + checks_si.cfg and FPGA\n    16\t// synth to fpga/core_bench_si.sv for this core. There is no channel 1.\n    17\t//\n    18\t// Latency:        full pipeline; instruction n retires at MEM/WB on\n    19\t//                 cycle n+4 (no hazards) or later (load-use stall,\n    20\t//                 redirect).\n    21\t// RVFI fields:    all of them — driven from the MEM/WB register and\n    22\t//                 the WB-stage write-data mux.\n    23\tmodule core (\n    24\t  input  logic        clock,\n    25\t  input  logic        reset,\n    26\t  // imem\n    27\t  output logic [31:0] io_imemAddr,\n    28\t  input  logic [31:0] io_imemData,\n    29\t  // imem bus backpressure. Drive 1 for zero-wait single-cycle BRAM (the\n    30\t  // V0 default). Drive 0 to model bus stall — PC reg holds, IF/ID\n    31\t  // payload becomes a NOP, and a pipeline bubble propagates downstream.\n    32\t  // Used by test/cosim/vex_main.cpp's --istall mode to match VexRiscv's\n    33\t  // random ~22% backpressure model so CoreMark/MHz can be compared\n    34\t  // apples-to-apples with their published \"full no cache\" number.\n    35\t  input  logic        io_imemReady,\n    36\t  // dmem\n    37\t  output logic [31:0] io_dmemAddr,\n    38\t  input  logic [31:0] io_dmemRData,\n    39\t  output logic [31:0] io_dmemWData,\n    40\t  output logic [3:0]  io_dmemWEn,\n    41\t  output lo\n…[7755 of 10827 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:39c17e87b4e98e56]…\n    io_rvfi_insn_0      = mem_wb_w.instr;\n   234\t    io_rvfi_trap_0      = mem_wb_w.ctrl.is_illegal;\n   235\t    io_rvfi_halt_0      = 1'b0;\n   236\t    io_rvfi_intr_0      = 1'b0;\n   237\t    io_rvfi_mode_0      = 2'd3;     // M-mode only\n   238\t    io_rvfi_ixl_0       = 2'd1;     // 32-bit ISA\n   239\t    io_rvfi_rs1_addr_0  = mem_wb_w.rs1_addr;\n   240\t    io_rvfi_rs1_rdata_0 = mem_wb_w.rs1_val;\n   241\t    io_rvfi_rs2_addr_0  = mem_wb_w.rs2_addr;\n   242\t    io_rvfi_rs2_rdata_0 = mem_wb_w.rs2_val;\n   243\t    io_rvfi_rd_addr_0   = rd_wen ? mem_wb_w.rd : 5'b0;\n   244\t    io_rvfi_rd_wdata_0  = rd_wen ? wb_w_data   : 32'b0;\n   245\t    io_rvfi_pc_rdata_0  = mem_wb_w.pc;\n   246\t    io_rvfi_pc_wdata_0  = mem_wb_w.pc_next;\n   247\t    io_rvfi_mem_addr_0  = mem_wb_w.mem_addr;\n   248\t    io_rvfi_mem_rmask_0 = mem_wb_w.mem_rmask;\n   249\t    io_rvfi_mem_wmask_0 = mem_wb_w.mem_wmask;\n   250\t    io_rvfi_mem_rdata_0 = mem_wb_w.mem_rdata;\n   251\t    io_rvfi_mem_wdata_0 = mem_wb_w.mem_wdata;\n   252\t  end\n   253\t\n   254\tendmodule\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
