{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"nl -ba cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv | sed -n '1,220p'\"", "aggregated_output": "     1\t// rtl/mem_stage.sv\n     2\t//\n     3\t// Memory access stage. Drives the dmem read/write ports combinationally\n     4\t// from the EX/MEM register, and sign/zero-extends the loaded data into\n     5\t// the MEM/WB register.\n     6\t//\n     7\t// Byte-lane discipline:\n     8\t//   - Write data is replicated across all four byte lanes; the\n     9\t//     byte-mask (mem_wmask) selects the actual destination bytes.\n    10\t//   - Load: shift the raw word right by `addr[1:0]*8`, then sign- or\n    11\t//     zero-extend the low 8/16 bits per the LB/LBU/LH/LHU encoding.\n    12\t//   - For RVFI ALIGNED_MEM, mem_addr is reported word-aligned and the\n    13\t//     byte position is captured in mem_rmask / mem_wmask.\n    14\t//\n    15\t// Latency:        1 cycle (MEM/WB register clocked here).\n    16\t// RVFI fields:    feeds mem_addr, mem_rmask, mem_wmask, mem_rdata,\n    17\t//                 mem_wdata, plus rd_wdata via the loaded-data path.\n    18\tmodule mem_stage (\n    19\t  input  logic               clock,\n    20\t  input  logic               reset,\n    21\t  // hold_wb: dmem stall is in effect. MEM/WB's data fields are RETAINED\n    22\t  // (so the previously-retired LOAD's `rd` / `read_data` / `ctrl.reg_write`\n    23\t  // remain visible to forward_unit), but `valid` is cleared so:\n    24\t  //   - rvfi_order doesn't increment for held cycles\n    25\t  //   - wb_stage doesn't write the regfile twice\n    26\t  // Zeroing the whole register would lose the LOAD's load_data, breaking\n    27\t  // MEM/WB->EX forwarding for any dependent instruction that's also held\n    28\t  // in ID/EX during the stall (e.g. a BNE that consumes a LOAD's result).\n    29\t  input  logic               hold_wb,\n    30\t  // ex_mem_t carries branch_taken / branch_target 