{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"test -f cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Posted store buffer implementation notes\n\nChanged RTL:\n- Added a one-entry posted data-RAM store buffer inside `mem_stage.sv`.\n- Bufferable stores are valid, aligned stores with byte address below\n  `0x0010_0000`. If such a store reaches MEM while `io_dmemReady` is low and\n  the buffer is empty, MEM captures address, replicated write data, and byte\n  mask into the buffer, lets the store retire through MEM/WB, and suppresses\n  the immediate dmem write enable for that not-ready cycle.\n- While occupied, the buffer owns the dmem write port until ready accepts it.\n  Younger loads/stores/memory traps wait behind it; younger non-memory\n  instructions can continue through MEM/WB.\n- Replaced hazard_unit's old blanket `!dmem_ready && ex_mem_mem_op` stall with\n  a `mem_stall` signal computed by MEM. Loads and non-bufferable stores still\n  block on dmem readiness.\n\nDeviations:\n- I kept the buffer inside `mem_stage.sv` rather than creating a separate\n  `store_buffer.sv`; the state and mux are small and tightly coupled to the\n  MEM dmem/RVFI metadata generation.\n- No pipeline bundle fields were widened. Bufferable classification is local\n  to MEM from the effective address, existing control bits, and alignment.\n\nConcerns:\n- The buffer path is not exercised by riscv-formal because the wrapper ties\n  dmem ready high. Cosim with random dmem stalls passed and is the meaningful\n  guard for this change.\n- The dmem output mux adds a small MEM-side timing cost; I did not run Gowin\n  timing locally.\n\nLocal checks:\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: pass.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass\n  (`Formal: 53 passed, 0 failed`).\n- Plain `make cosim TARGET=bench` initially failed before simulation because\n  this Makefile path did not pass `NRET=1` to the harness. Rerun with the\n  core's declared RVFI width:\n  `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass (`elfs_tested: 2`).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
