{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"I’ve found the current design still has the textbook one-cycle load-use detector feeding a bubble, and forwarding only distinguishes EX/MEM ALU data vs MEM/WB writeback. The shape is friendly for a small change: add one extra “MEM load” forwarding select, and let the existing dmem stall remain the only memory wait path."}}
