{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_77","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Retire shadow forwarding implementation notes\n\nWhat changed:\n- Removed the write-first same-cycle bypass from `rtl/reg_file.sv`; reads now return only x0 or the stored register word.\n- Added a retired-write shadow in `rtl/core.sv` and wired it into the existing EX operand forwarding path.\n- Extended `rtl/forward_unit.sv` and `rtl/ex_stage.sv` with forwarding select `2'd3` for the shadow source, below EX/MEM and MEM/WB priority.\n- Added a small pending slot for WB writes that occur while ID/EX is held by dmem or divider stalls. The active shadow is preserved for the held instruction, then refreshed with the newest held-off WB write once the backend advances.\n- Updated regfile tests for stored-value read semantics and added a pipeline test covering the former WB-to-ID write-first dependency.\n\nDeviations:\n- The basic shadow register needed one extra pending entry. A first version that overwrote the shadow during backend stalls passed lint/formal but failed stalled CoreMark because a held ID/EX consumer could lose the older same-cycle WB value it still needed.\n\nConcerns:\n- The pending slot is intentionally tiny and only tracks the newest held-off WB write. That is sufficient because the active shadow is only needed by the currently held ID/EX instruction; future instructions can read older held-off writes from the regfile after the hold releases, while the newest pending write becomes the next shadow candidate.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench` by itself builds the harness with default `NRET=2` in this checkout, while `cores/bench/core.yaml` declares `nret: 1`. The orchestrator path injects `NRET=1`; local cosim was therefore run as `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`.\n\nLocal status:\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- Cocotb regfile/pipeline runners: pass.\n- Formal: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed.\n- Cosim: pass with `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_78","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented retire shadow forwarding in `cores/bench`.\n\nChanged:\n- Removed regfile write-first bypass.\n- Added retained WB shadow plus pending held-write slot in `core.sv`.\n- Added shadow forwarding source in `forward_unit.sv` and `ex_stage.sv`.\n- Updated regfile test and added the focused WB-to-ID RAW pipeline test.\n- Wrote `cores/bench/implementation_notes.md`.\n\nChecks:\n- Verilator lint: passed.\n- Cocotb regfile/pipeline runners: passed.\n- Formal: passed, `53 passed, 0 failed`.\n- Cosim: passed with `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`.\n\nNote: bare `make cosim TARGET=bench` builds the local harness with default `NRET=2` here, which conflicts with this core’s `nret: 1`; the evaluator path injects `NRET=1`."}}
