{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Split execute address lane\n==========================\n\nWhat changed:\n- Added a dedicated `rs1 + imm` address/control lane in `rtl/ex_stage.sv`.\n- JALR redirect target generation now uses that lane.\n- LOAD/STORE instructions now place the address-lane sum into the EX/MEM result field consumed by `mem_stage`, instead of using the general ALU result mux.\n- General ALU/MUL/DIV behavior and pipeline depth are unchanged. JAL/JALR still write `pc + 4` through the existing EX/MEM result path.\n- Added cocotb pipeline coverage for immediately forwarded base registers into LW, SW, and JALR.\n\nDeviations:\n- No new execute-result metadata was added in `core_pkg.sv`; the existing `ctrl.mem_read`, `ctrl.mem_write`, and `ctrl.is_jalr` bits were enough to select the address lane locally in EX.\n- `mem_stage.sv` was left unchanged so the downstream memory/RVFI contract remains the same.\n\nConcerns:\n- The EX/MEM field is still named `alu_result` even though memory ops now carry an address-lane result in it. Renaming it would touch more files for little structural benefit.\n- Plain `make cosim TARGET=bench` defaults the C++ harness to `NRET=2` and fails to compile against this `nret: 1` core. `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` matches `cores/bench/core.yaml` and passes.\n\nLocal verification:\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: pass.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed.\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py`: pass.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, 2 ELF files tested.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
