{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_14", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -n 20 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-003-r7s2\", \"title\": \"Decode-stage direct-jump predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Prior predictor attempts on this core all lost when they added tag\\nlookup, immediate generation, pattern matching, or repair state to the\\nlive fetch path.  The lowest-risk remaining predictor is the static\\narchitectural fact that direct JAL is always taken and its target is\\navailable from the existing decode-stage immediate generator.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Prior predictor attempts on this core all lost when they added tag\\nlookup, immediate generation, pattern matching, or repair state to the\\nlive fetch path.  The lowest-risk remaining predictor is the static\\narchitectural fact that direct JAL is always taken and its target is\\navailable from the existing decode-stage immediate generator.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a narrow decode-stage direct-jump predictor for JAL only.  When the\\ncurrent fetched instruction is a valid JAL, imem is ready, decode is not\\nbeing stalled or flushed, and the computed JAL target is word-aligned, ID\\nredirects the fetch PC to pc+imm at the same clock edge that the JAL enters\\nID/EX.  Carry a single predicted-direct-jump bit in ID/EX so EX suppresses\\nthe normal JAL redirect when the early prediction was used; branches and\\nJALR remain on the existing EX-resolution path.\\n\\nThis should remove one wrong-path fetch bubble from every correctly aligned\\ndirect call or jump without a BTB, fetch-side target adder, saturating\\ncounter, return stack, or predictor table.  The added logic is a single\\nJAL opcode check, reuse of ID's immediate/pc adder, one PC-select input in\\nIF, and one suppress bit in EX, so it targets CoreMark call/control-flow\\nbubbles while avoiding the predictor structures that hurt Fmax in earlier\\nrounds.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a predicted_direct_jump bit to the ID/EX bundle so EX can distinguish a JAL already redirected by decode from\n…[100664 of 103736 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8a511f0d5dfa5a17]…\n\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 110.07, \"delta_pct\": -8.47, \"vs_baseline\": 808.17, \"fmax_mhz\": 49.44, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491817, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2777, \"ff\": 722, \"seeds\": [48.772, 49.44, 49.44], \"perturbations\": [[0, 48.772, 14], [1, 49.44, 14], [2, 49.44, 14]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_2_dmem_2_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -15.503, \"arrival_ns\": 25.798, \"logic_cells\": 14, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 14, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T20:06:10.005219Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 14, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-001-r14s0 (regression, -8.47%): Moving JAL/JALR link selection from EX to WB saved a rare jump-result mux but added a `pc + 4` adder and `is_jump` select to the shared `wb_w_data` forwarding path, so late writeback mux cost outweighed EX result-path cleanup.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
