{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261003-002-r5s1/.agent.last\"","aggregated_output":"Implemented the posted store buffer in MEM.\n\nChanged:\n- [mem_stage.sv](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261003-002-r5s1/cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv): one-entry buffer for aligned data-RAM stores below `0x0010_0000`, dmem output mux, MEM-local stall decision.\n- [hazard_unit.sv](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261003-002-r5s1/cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv): consumes MEM’s `mem_stall` instead of blanket dmem freeze.\n- [core.sv](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-5_5_xhigh-v2-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261003-002-r5s1/cores/bench/rtl/core.sv): wired `dmem_ready` and `mem_stall`.\n\nVerification:\n- Lint: pass.\n- Formal: pass, `53 passed, 0 failed`.\n- Cosim: `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` pass, `elfs_tested: 2`.\n\nNote: plain `make cosim TARGET=bench` in this checkout invoked the harness with `NRET=2` and failed before simulation because this core is `nret: 1`; rerunning with `NRET=1` matches the declared core contract. Implementation notes are in `cores/bench/implementation_notes.md`.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
