ming.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:9:- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r3s2 (regression, -13.86%): Even an EX-trained one-entry backedge predictor keeps a PC tag compare/target mux in IF and adds `pred_next_pc` mismatch plumbing through ID/EX, so CoreMark's loop-bubble savings still lost to fetch/control-path timing \n…[60084 of 63156 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0f5b40e1ec13aa66]…\nsion\", \"fitness\": 109.78, \"delta_pct\": -4.21, \"vs_baseline\": 805.78, \"fmax_mhz\": 49.309, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491817, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2498, \"ff\": 648, \"seeds\": [46.097, 49.309, 49.309], \"perturbations\": [[0, 46.097, 15], [1, 49.309, 13], [2, 49.309, 13]], \"lutram\": 0, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"dmem_2_dmem_2_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -16.693, \"arrival_ns\": 26.988, \"logic_cells\": 15, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 15, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T17:22:29.255740Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-001-r5s0 (regression, -4.21%): Removing the regfile x1..x31 synchronous clear did not relieve the reported ER-control endpoint, suggesting Gowin's reset/enable packing was not the real CoreMark limiter and the surrounding ID/EX/IF control/routing dominated instead.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
