{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json, re, sys\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r10s0.yaml')\ntext=p.read_text()\nprint(text)\ntry:\n    import yaml\n    data=yaml.safe_load(text)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print('YAML_LOAD_ERROR', e)\n    sys.exit(1)\nprint('loaded id:', data.get('id'))\nprint('category:', data.get('category'))\nprint('impact type:', type(data.get('expected_impact',{}).get('fitness_delta_pct')).__name__)\nfor c in data.get('changes',[]):\n    ok=bool(re.match(r'\"'^(rtl/[''^.].*|test/test_[''^/]+'\"\\\\.py)\"'$'\"', c.get('file','')))\n    print(c.get('file'), 'regex_ok=', ok)\n    if not ok: sys.exit(2)\ntry:\n    import jsonschema\n    schema=json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text())\n    jsonschema.validate(data, schema)\n    print('jsonschema: OK')\nexcept ModuleNotFoundError:\n    print('jsonschema: unavailable, regex/type checks passed')\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print('SCHEMA_ERROR', e)\n    sys.exit(3)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r10s0\ntitle: \"Offload high-half multiplies\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion is no longer limited by the old combinational divider, and\n  later attempts show that adding fetch prediction, broader predecode, new bypass\n  paths, or duplicate address lanes usually costs more timing than it saves. The\n  remaining hot paths still pass through the EX ALU region, where the fast path\n  carries three 32x32 multiplier products even though CoreMark primarily benefits\n  from keeping ordinary MUL single-cycle.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep ALU_MUL as a single-cycle DSP-backed low-half multiply, but remove\n  MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU from the common combinational ALU result path. Handle\n  those high-half multiply opcodes with a small multi-cycle execute-side unit\n  that captures operands, computes the signed/unsigned high half off the normal\n  ALU mux, and reuses the existing divider-style pipeline hold until the result\n  is ready. DIV/REM behavior, ALTOPS substitutions, branch timing, load/store\n  timing, and the top-level nret=1 contract stay unchanged.\n\n  This avoids the failed all-MUL multi-cycle tradeoff by preserving CoreMark's\n  useful single-cycle MUL throughput, and avoids the failed combinational shared\n  high-multiply correction path by not putting sign-correction carry chains after\n  the DSP output on every cycle. If CoreMark rarely executes high-half multiply\n  instructions, IPC should remain effectively flat while the reduced DSP/mux\n  pressure in the EX ALU cone improves median Tang Nano 20K Fmax.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Keep only the low-half MUL product in the combinational ALU fast path; make real MULH/MULHU/MULHSU results come from the execute-side multi-cycle unit while preserving ALTOPS behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add high-half multiply busy/done/result handling beside the existing divider control and select the completed high-multiply result into EX/MEM.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Treat high-half multiply busy cycles like the existing divider busy stall so IF and ID hold while MEM/WB drains.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the generalized execute busy signal through the existing hazard path without changing top-level IO.\"\n  - file: rtl/mulh_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add a compact multi-cycle unit for MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU with exact RV32M signed and unsigned high-half semantics.\"\n\nloaded id: hyp-20261003-001-r10s0\ncategory: micro_opt\nimpact type: int\nrtl/alu.sv regex_ok= True\nrtl/ex_stage.sv regex_ok= True\nrtl/hazard_unit.sv regex_ok= True\nrtl/core.sv regex_ok= True\nrtl/mulh_unit.sv regex_ok= True\njsonschema: OK\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
