{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r11s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r11s0\ntitle: \"Register memory lane sideband\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current best design has already removed the large divider path and\n  registered the forwarding plan, so the remaining timing reports are short\n  cones through ID/EX, the ALU region, and the dmem-facing port logic. Prior\n  attempts that added prediction, extra bypasses, or duplicate address lanes\n  usually lost to routing and control cost. A narrower target is the MEM-stage\n  byte-lane/misalignment logic: every load/store currently rebuilds byte masks,\n  replicated store data, and alignment predicates from EX/MEM address/control\n  bits directly in front of the timed dmem BRAM interface.\nhypothesis: |\n  Move the dmem byte-lane sideband calculation to the execute handoff and carry\n  compact registered fields in EX/MEM: replicated store data, byte mask, and a\n  precomputed memory-misaligned flag. MEM can then drive io_dmemWData,\n  io_dmemWEn, io_dmemREn, RVFI masks, and trap gating from registered sideband\n  rather than recomputing shifts, width decodes, and alignment compares on the\n  same cycle as the dmem port setup. Keep the effective address itself in the\n  existing ALU result field, preserve all RV32I misalignment trap behavior, and\n  leave load extraction after dmem read unchanged.\n\n  This should reduce LUT depth and routing on the memory-side critical cone\n  without adding new pipeline stages, predictors, or CoreMark cycle cost. The\n  risk is that moving mask generation earlier adds some ALU-to-EX/MEM setup\n  work, but it is only small decode/mux logic and it replaces equivalent logic\n  now sitting directly on the dmem-facing timed path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add registered memory sideband fields to ex_mem_t for replicated store data, byte mask, and memory-misaligned status.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute load/store byte mask, replicated store data, and misalignment from the ALU effective address and decoded memory width before latching EX/MEM.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Drive dmem write data, write enables, read enable, RVFI masks, and trap gating from the registered sideband instead of rebuilding the logic in MEM.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Update the forwarding misalignment kill to use the registered EX/MEM memory-misaligned sideband while preserving existing load-use and stall behavior.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add focused tests for byte, halfword, word, and misaligned load/store cases to guard the relocated sideband logic.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
