{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r13s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r13s0\ntitle: \"Bias ALU mux for add path\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current accepted core is still limited by a short path through ID/EX,\n  the EX operand muxes, rtl/alu.sv, and the MEM-facing result/address cone.\n  CoreMark's hottest timed uses of that cone are ordinary ADD-family results\n  and load/store effective addresses, but the current ALU presents ADD as one\n  arm of a broad RV32IM result case that also includes shifts, compares, LUI,\n  and single-cycle MUL-class results. Prior attempts to add a separate fast\n  add slice regressed because they widened ID/EX control and duplicated\n  datapath routing; the remaining lower-risk target is the mux shape inside\n  the existing ALU boundary.\nhypothesis: |\n  Restructure rtl/alu.sv as a hot-path-biased mux tree without changing the\n  ALU interface, pipeline state, op encodings, or any instruction latency.\n  Compute the ADD/SUB carry-chain result once, select ALU_ADD (and optionally\n  ALU_SUB) through an explicit first-level two-way path, and put the residual\n  operations behind a separate non-add case tree. Keep the existing DSP-backed\n  MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU behavior and the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutions\n  bit-identical, but keep their result muxing off the common ADD/address data\n  path as much as the Gowin mapper will honor.\n\n  This should preserve CoreMark cycles while shaving one or more LUT/mux\n  levels from the RF/forwarding-to-ALU-to-dmem path that dominates recent\n  timing reports. Unlike the failed fast-add sideband attempts, it adds no new\n  ID/EX bits, no duplicate adder, no memory sideband register, and no predictor\n  repair plumbing; the risk is mainly that synthesis flattens the mux back to\n  the old shape, in which case the circuit should remain functionally neutral.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Refactor the combinational ALU into an explicit ADD/SUB fast selection followed by a residual case tree for logic, shifts, compares, LUI, MUL-class operations, DIV/REM placeholders, and ALTOPS formulas.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Retain or extend focused ALU vectors around ADD/SUB, shifts, comparisons, MUL-class results, and ALTOPS-sensitive divide placeholders to guard the mux refactor.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
