{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,200p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r14s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r14s0\ntitle: \"Gate redirect on valid EX ops\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  Recent timing reports keep landing on a short but stubborn loop from regfile\n  data through ID/EX, EX branch/jump redirect generation, IF flush/PC control,\n  and back into decode/regfile-facing control. Several attempts to add new\n  predictors or duplicate address/add paths lost because they widened routing.\n  A lower-risk target is the existing EX redirect signal itself: invalid\n  bubbles currently still drive the full branch/jump compare and target-control\n  cone even though they can never architecturally redirect.\nhypothesis: |\n  Qualify all EX-stage redirect work with the ID/EX valid bit as early as\n  possible. In ex_stage, form an ex_valid control and use it to gate\n  branch_taken, jump redirect generation, misalignment target-trap detection,\n  and the exported redirect signal. For invalid bubbles, the branch comparator,\n  jump selection, and redirect fanout should collapse to constants, reducing\n  toggling and giving Gowin a simpler control cone from forwarded/regfile\n  operands into IF/hazard/regfile enable logic.\n\n  This does not add pipeline state, predictors, sideband adders, or new memory\n  behavior. Valid instructions keep identical pc_next, trap, writeback, DIV/REM,\n  and RVFI behavior; only architecturally dead invalid-cycle control is pruned.\n  The expected benefit is a modest Fmax lift on the current dominant control\n  path with unchanged CoreMark cycles.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Gate branch_taken, jump redirect, misalignment redirect/trap checks, and exported redirect with in.valid so invalid bubbles do not exercise the full EX-to-IF control cone.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Preserve existing stall and flush priority while relying on the already-qualified redirect input; no new state or bus behavior is added.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Keep top-level wiring unchanged except for any local naming needed to document that redirect is valid-qualified before feeding IF and hazard logic.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
