{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n \\\"regs_ER|ER_s|regfile|reg_file|u_rf|critical path|worst path\\\" cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl cores/bench/implementation_notes.md cores/bench -g '\"'!rtl/*.sv'\"'\"", "aggregated_output": "rg: cores/bench/implementation_notes.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Iterative divider off ALU critical path\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current timed path runs from the forwarding logic through EX and the\\ncombinational ALU, with roughly 150 logic levels. The ALU implements RV32M\\nDIV/REM using SystemVerilog / and %, forcing Gowin to time a full\\nsingle-cycle divider/remainder network even though CoreMark rarely needs\\nthose operations in the measured loop. Removing that arithmetic from the\\none-cycle EX path should raise Fmax far more than the occasional multi-cycle\\ndivide can hurt iterations per cycle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current timed path runs from the forwarding logic through EX and the\\ncombinational ALU, with roughly 150 logic levels. The ALU implements RV32M\\nDIV/REM using SystemVerilog / and %, forcing Gowin to time a full\\nsingle-cycle divider/remainder network even though CoreMark rarely needs\\nthose operations in the measured loop. Removing that arithmetic from the\\none-cycle EX path should raise Fmax far more than the occasional multi-cycle\\ndivide can hurt iterations per cycle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU cases in rtl/alu.sv with a small\\niterative divider/remainder unit that is invoked only when the decoded ALU op\\nis one of the four divide-class RV32M operations. EX holds the pipeline while\\nthe unit is busy, then writes the final quotient or remainder into the normal\\nEX/MEM register with unchanged RVFI contents. Keep MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU on\\nthe existing combinational/DSP path and preserve the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\\nsubstitutions. This should turn the common ADD/compare/address critical path\\nback into a short mux-plus-adder path, reduce divider LUT depth, and improve\\nmedian Tang Nano 20K Fmax enough to clear the acceptance threshold.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 18, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu\n…[113287 of 116359 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f08eb14a307f42a1]…\n \"logic_levels\": 34, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T17:11:26.225166Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 4, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r4s2 (regression, -28.11%): Retiming a tiny BTB into a registered lookahead still adds IF table update/lookup state plus `pred_pc_next` compare plumbing through ID/EX, so avoiding same-cycle PC-select compares did not make CoreMark's taken-branch bubble savings worth the extra fetch/control cost.\"}\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py:1:\"\"\"Unit tests for rtl/reg_file.sv. Covers x0 hardwiring, write-first\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py:96:def test_reg_file_runner():\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py:97:    run_cocotb(toplevel=\"reg_file\",\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py:98:               sources=[\"reg_file.sv\"],\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py:99:               test_module=\"test_reg_file\")\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py:370:            \"alu.sv\", \"decoder.sv\", \"imm_gen.sv\", \"reg_file.sv\",\n", "exit_code": 2, "status": "failed"}}
