{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r5s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r5s0\ntitle: \"Remove regfile bulk reset\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion's median timing path no longer points at DIV/REM or\n  branch prediction logic; it terminates in the register file's FPGA ER\n  control after passing through ID, EX, and IF. The regfile still synchronously\n  clears all 32 architectural registers on reset even though RV32I only\n  requires x0 to read as zero and the benchmark CRT initializes its live\n  software state explicitly. That reset fanout and enable/reset control can be\n  timed even though it does no useful work during CoreMark.\nhypothesis: |\n  Remove the synchronous clear of the writable x1..x31 register storage in\n  rtl/reg_file.sv while keeping x0 hardwired to zero, write suppression for x0,\n  and the existing same-cycle write-first bypass. Leave the reset input present\n  or locally lint-suppressed so the top-level wiring need not change, but do\n  not feed reset into every GPR bit. Update the local cocotb regfile test to\n  stop requiring non-architectural reset-to-zero behavior and instead verify\n  x0, normal writes after reset, dual reads, and write-first bypass.\n\n  This should directly attack the current regfile ER/control endpoint and\n  remove a high-fanout reset tree from 31x32 bits without adding any pipeline\n  state or changing CoreMark cycles. If Gowin can pack the regfile as simpler\n  distributed storage or flops with only write enables, the Fmax gain can be\n  large enough to clear the acceptance threshold while preserving RVFI and ISA\n  behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/reg_file.sv\n    description: \"Drop the synchronous reset clear for x1..x31, keep x0 hardwired and write-first bypass semantics, and avoid introducing reset into the read/write datapath.\"\n  - file: test/test_reg_file.py\n    description: \"Replace the reset-clears-all unit expectation with architectural checks that writes after reset work, x0 remains zero, both read ports function, and write-first bypass is preserved.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
