{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20261003-001-r3s0\\\") | {id,title,motivation,hypothesis:.hypothesis.hypothesis,expected_impact,changes,outcome,fitness,fmax_mhz,critical_path,lesson} | tostring' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\":\"hyp-20261003-001-r3s0\",\"title\":\"Move IF bubbles into ID\",\"motivation\":\"The current champion is no longer limited by the RV32M divider; its worst\\npath runs through the ID/EX redirect cone, IF bubble generation, and back\\ntoward the regfile/decode side. The prior raw-rs hazard change removed the\\nIF flush-to-NOP mux from load-use detection, but the same 32-bit mux still\\nfeeds the ID decoder and register-file read addresses on every redirect or\\nimem stall.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Keep the lightweight combinational IF/ID boundary, but stop muxing the full\\nfetched instruction to ADDI x0,x0,0 in if_stage. Instead, carry raw imemData\\nwith an explicit valid bit, make id_stage turn invalid fetches into a zeroed\\nID/EX bubble, and drive x0/x0 regfile read addresses when the IF payload is\\ninvalid. Also qualify EX redirect generation with in.valid so any invalid\\npayload cannot affect the PC if control bits are zeroed late. This should\\nshorten the EX redirect/imem-stall to IF to regfile/decode timing cone from\\na 32-bit instruction mux plus decode fanout to a narrow valid/address gate,\\npreserving CoreMark IPC while improving median Fmax.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":6,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Remove the redirect/flush-to-NOP instruction mux from the IF output; emit raw imem data plus the existing valid indication.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Convert invalid IF payloads into a zeroed ID/EX bubble and gate regfile read addresses to x0 when fetch valid is low.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Qualify redirect and redirect_target selection with in.valid so invalid bubbles cannot steer fetch.\"}],\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"fitness\":112.7,\"fmax_mhz\":50.621,\"critical_path\":{\"from\":\"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\",\"to\":\"cpu/u_rf/regs_ER_s195\",\"slack_ns\":-15.186,\"arrival_ns\":25.481,\"logic_cells\":34,\"modules\":[\"clock_ibuf\",\"cpu/u_id\",\"cpu/u_ex\",\"cpu/u_if\",\"cpu/u_id\",\"cpu/u_rf\"]},\"lesson\":\"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-001-r3s0 (regression, -1.67%): After raw-rs load-use gating, removing IF's flush-to-NOP instruction mux only moved bubble control into `in.valid` gates on ID regfile addresses, ID/EX zeroing, and EX redirect qualification, so the added valid fanout did not buy CoreMark timing relief.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
