"title\": \"Iterative divider off ALU critical path\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current timed path runs from the forwarding logic through EX and the\\ncombinational ALU, with roughly 150 logic levels. The ALU implements RV32M\\nDIV/REM using SystemVerilog / and %, forcing Gowin to time a full\\nsingl\n…[46597 of 49669 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e610fb281039d58e]…\nd.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the blanket dmem-store freeze with stalls only for loads, non-bufferable stores, or any memory op that would conflict with an occupied store buffer.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire store-buffer full/drain status between MEM and hazard control while preserving the existing nret=1 IO and RVFI retirement contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add any small control bit needed to identify bufferable data-RAM stores without widening unrelated pipeline paths.\"}], \"outcome\": \"placement_failed\", \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": \"placement_failed\", \"seeds\": [null, null, null], \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-002-r5s1 (placement_failed, n/a): Posting dmem stores by muxing a buffered writer onto the byte-lane write port can break Gowin BRAM inference for the FPGA wrapper's 8 KiB dmem, falling back to per-lane DFF memory and exhausting FF resources before timing is measured.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
