{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r6s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r6s0\ntitle: \"Opcode-aware load-use stalls\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion already shortened the load-use timing loop by feeding\n  the hazard unit from raw imem register fields. It still conservatively treats\n  both raw rs fields as real sources for every fetched instruction. That can\n  insert false one-cycle bubbles after loads when the following instruction is\n  OP-IMM, LOAD, JALR, LUI, AUIPC, JAL, or FENCE and a non-source bit field\n  happens to equal the load destination.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep the existing combinational fetch/decode boundary and raw-imem hazard\n  path, but add a tiny opcode-only source-use predecode for the fetched word.\n  LOAD, OP-IMM, and JALR should compare only rs1; LUI, AUIPC, JAL, and FENCE\n  should compare neither source; OP, STORE, and BRANCH should compare both.\n  Unknown or trap-prone opcode classes can remain conservative. The load-use\n  stall then fires only when the load destination matches a source operand the\n  next instruction will actually consume.\n\n  This should reduce CoreMark cycles by eliminating spurious load-use bubbles\n  without adding predictor state, extra pipeline registers, or memory-port\n  muxing. The added opcode mask is much smaller than the failed fetch-buffer\n  and predictor logic, and it can be computed in parallel with the existing\n  raw rs extraction so the Fmax risk should be modest.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Derive opcode-only fetch_uses_rs1/fetch_uses_rs2 bits from io_imemData and pass them with the existing raw source fields into the hazard unit.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Gate the load-use compare with fetched source-use bits so stalls are emitted only for true consumer operands, while keeping invalid fetch, redirect kill, dmem stall, and divider busy priority unchanged.\"\n  - file: test/test_hazard_unit.py\n    description: \"Add focused cocotb cases proving OP-IMM/LOAD/JAL/LUI-style non-source fields do not trigger false load-use stalls, while OP/STORE/BRANCH true dependencies still stall.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
