{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r8s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r8s0\ntitle: \"Specialize branch EX fast path\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion's timing is dominated by the decode/register-file through EX redirect/front-end feedback region, and prior attempts show that adding predictors, skid buffers, load bypasses, or broad ID precompute usually costs more routing than it saves. The best near-miss was precomputing PC-relative values in ID, which improved Fmax but missed the acceptance threshold because it widened ID/EX and added decode-stage adders.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep the existing 5-stage behavior and raw-imem load-use detection, but specialize the EX branch/jump cone instead of moving work into ID. Add a small branch/jump target adder beside the main ALU and route conditional-branch/JAL target generation directly from `in.pc + in.imm`, while the main ALU is reserved for register arithmetic, load/store effective addresses, AUIPC, LUI, and MUL-class results. Use a separate `pc_plus4 = in.pc + 4` adder for JAL/JALR link data and fall-through RVFI pc_next, and select branch/JALR redirect/pc_next from these dedicated results.\n\n  This aims to remove the branch/jump target and link-data muxing from the already-wide ALU result cone without adding predictor state, same-cycle ID-to-IF redirection, or extra ID/EX payload. It should behave like the current core cycle-for-cycle, but give Gowin more freedom to place a short redirect path and a short ALU/writeback path separately.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Split branch/JAL target and PC+4 link/fall-through adders out of the main ALU result cone, then use the dedicated results for redirect, pc_next, and jump writeback while preserving existing divider and misalignment behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Keep the ALU interface and RV32IM results intact, but allow EX to bypass the ALU result for control-flow link/target values so ordinary arithmetic and memory-address timing is less coupled to branch redirect logic.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
