{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r8s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r8s0\ntitle: \"Dedicated load-store address adder\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion's timing is dominated by the decode/register-file through EX/front-end region, and several recent worst paths still pass through `cpu/u_ex/u_alu` before reaching dmem-facing logic. Prior attempts show that adding predictor state, skid buffering, or broad ID precompute costs more than it saves, while moving MUL out of the single-cycle path hurts CoreMark throughput. A narrower EX datapath specialization that preserves IPC is the most promising remaining micro-opt.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep the existing pipeline, stall behavior, divider, and single-cycle multiply path, but add a dedicated 32-bit effective-address adder in EX for LOAD and STORE instructions. Today memory operations compute `rs1 + imm` through the full ALU module and then carry that result into EX/MEM, so dmem address timing pays for the ALU case muxing and nearby M-extension result cone even though memory ops only need addition. For `ctrl.mem_read || ctrl.mem_write`, select the dedicated address-adder result into `reg_q.alu_result`; all arithmetic, AUIPC/LUI, jumps, branches, and M-extension instructions keep their existing ALU/redirect behavior.\n\n  CoreMark's timed loop is load/store heavy, and the FPGA score uses randomized dmem stalls, so shortening the address path into the memory stage can improve median Fmax without changing iterations/cycle. The change avoids new IF control, extra ID/EX payload, or multi-cycle arithmetic; it just lets Gowin place the common memory-address adder separately from the wider ALU result mux.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a dedicated effective-address adder fed by the forwarded rs1 value and immediate, and select it into EX/MEM alu_result for LOAD/STORE operations while preserving all existing redirect, jump, divider, and RVFI behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
