{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r9s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r9s0\ntitle: \"One-hot fast ALU selects\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion is no longer dominated by the removed combinational divider; recent timing reports repeatedly land in the decode/register-file through EX/ALU cone, often ending at dmem-facing logic. Prior micro-opts that added fetch prediction, buffering, load bypassing, or duplicate address adders either added control delay or failed to isolate the path. The remaining opportunity is to make the existing single-cycle EX datapath cheaper without changing pipeline timing or CoreMark's useful single-cycle multiply behavior.\nhypothesis: |\n  Recode the ALU control path from a compact 5-bit binary operation plus large case decode inside rtl/alu.sv into a small predecoded/one-hot set of operation enables carried in the existing ID/EX control bundle. The decoder can expand the opcode/funct match once in ID, while EX uses direct enables for the fast integer groups: add/sub/address, logic, shifts, signed/unsigned compares, LUI, and M-extension result selects. DIV/REM continue to use the existing iterative divider path, and MUL-class operations remain single-cycle DSP operations.\n\n  This should remove several 5-bit equality comparators and a wide binary case-select tree from the RF/forwarding-to-ALU-result path that now limits Fmax, replacing them with local one-hot muxing that Gowin can pack more predictably. Because the instruction schedule, branch timing, memory stall behavior, divider behavior, and multiplier latency are unchanged, iterations/cycle should stay essentially flat; the hoped-for gain is purely median Fmax.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Replace or augment the compact alu_op field with predecoded one-hot ALU operation enables in ctrl_t, keeping the pipeline and nret=1 IO contract unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n    description: \"Generate the one-hot ALU enables directly from the existing validated opcode/funct arms while preserving the illegal-default decoder discipline.\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Use one-hot operation enables to select fast integer, shift, compare, LUI, and MUL results with a shallower mux structure; keep ALTOPS substitutions and real DIV/REM exclusion intact.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Update ALU instantiation and divide-op detection to consume the predecoded control bits without changing forwarding, redirects, divider stalls, or EX/MEM register behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
