{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20261003-001-r7s0\\\") | \\\"ID: \\\\(.id)\\\\nTITLE: \\\\(.title)\\\\nOUTCOME: \\\\(.outcome) delta \\\\(.delta_pct)% fitness \\\\(.fitness) fmax \\\\(.fmax_mhz) cycles \\\\(.cycles)\\\\nHYPOTHESIS:\\\\n\\\\(.hypothesis.hypothesis // .hypothesis)\\\\nLESSON:\\\\n\\\\(.lesson // \\\"\\\")\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"ID: hyp-20261003-001-r7s0\nTITLE: Precompute branch targets in ID\nOUTCOME: regression delta 3.7% fitness 118.85 fmax 53.384 cycles 4491817\nHYPOTHESIS:\nPrecompute the common PC-relative next-PC values in ID and carry them as\nregistered fields in id_ex_t. Specifically, have id_stage calculate pc_plus4\nand pc_imm_target = pc + imm, then make ex_stage use those registered values\nfor conditional branch targets, JAL targets, JAL/JALR link data, and RVFI\npc_next wherever the current code recomputes in.pc + 4 or in.pc + in.imm.\nJALR still needs the rs1 + imm adder in EX, but CoreMark's hot conditional\nbranches and direct jumps should no longer put two PC adders in the same EX\nredirect/pc_next cone.\n\nThis should preserve IPC, the simple combinational IF/ID boundary, and the\ncurrent load-use behavior while shortening the branch/jump timing path that\nfeeds IF. The cost is only a pair of 32-bit ID/EX registers and one ID-stage\nadder that is off the reported EX-to-IF critical loop.\n\nLESSON:\n- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-001-r7s0 (regression, +3.70%): Precomputing `pc_plus4`/`pc_imm_target` in ID regressed because the added ID adders and 64 bits of ID/EX payload sit on the already-sensitive decode/regfile/control routing, while EX redirect still needs branch/JALR mux/control work.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"One near miss is important: precomputing PC+4 and PC+imm in ID reached 118.85 fitness, about 3.7% over the champion but below the 4.6% acceptance guard. I’m going to use that as negative-positive evidence: the PC-side redirect cone can improve Fmax, but broad ID adders and extra ID/EX payload are just barely too expensive."}}
