lementation must hold the registered wb_data, rd, and compact writeback\n  control when MEM/WB valid is cleared during a memory wait.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Reshape mem_wb_t to carry compact registered writeback fields such as wb_data, wb_en, rd, trap, and the existing RVFI memory metadata instead of a full late-use ctrl_t plus separate writeback sources.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Select and latch final rd writeback data/control at the MEM/WB boundary, and retain those fields during dmem hold cycles for MEM/WB forwarding.\"\n  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n    description: \"Drive w_en, w_addr, and w_data directly from the compact registered MEM/WB writeback slice so WB no longer contains a live mem_to_reg data mux.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Forward the registered WB value into EX and map the compact MEM/WB trap/writeback fields onto RVFI without changing any top-level ports.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add focused RAW tests for ALU results, loads, and dmem-stalled load-use forwarding to catch stale registered writeback values.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
