is should turn the common ADD/compare/address critical path\\nback into a short mux-plus-adder path, reduce divider LUT depth, and improve\\nmedian Tang Nano 20K Fmax enough to clear the acceptance threshold.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 18, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real DIV/REM operators from the combinational ALU path, leaving only simple ALU ops a\n…[158958 of 162030 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:544165143cf9bbf4]…\n\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4456219, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2804, \"ff\": 657, \"seeds\": [49.002, 50.182, 50.182], \"perturbations\": [[0, 49.002, 21], [1, 50.182, 20], [2, 50.182, 20]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/pc_7_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -15.408, \"arrival_ns\": 25.702, \"logic_cells\": 47, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_id/u_imm\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 21, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T19:02:54.198885Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 11, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r11s2 (regression, -6.35%): Narrowing decode-stage JAL prediction to aligned `jal x0` still leaves the ID `pc + imm` target adder, same-cycle ID-to-IF PC-select path, ID/EX marker bit, and EX redirect suppression in sensitive control routing, so CoreMark's unconditional-direct-jump bubble savings were too sparse to pay back the Fmax loss.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
