operations no longer reuse the full ALU/writeback result path for dmem addressing.\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Expose the ADD-side result used for address generation separately from the final ALU operation result, preserving RV32M and ALTOPS behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the effective memory address from the ALU add side-output into EX/MEM while leaving alu_result as the register-writeback result.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Drive dmem_addr, aligned RVFI mem_addr, masks, load extraction shifts, and misalignment checks from the registered memory-address field for memory ops.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Update forwarding misalignment kill logic to use the registered memory address path without changing stall, divider, or RVFI top-level behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
