{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r4s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-002-r4s1\ntitle: \"Two-entry fetch skid buffer\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion has already removed the dominant divider path and the\n  failed IF/ID and predictor attempts show that adding latency or fetch-side\n  target logic is too expensive. However, the benchmark still drives about 22%\n  random instruction-bus stalls, and the existing front end can only fetch the\n  instruction currently being decoded. When the backend is stalled by dmem,\n  load-use bubbles, or the iterative divider, those cycles cannot be used to\n  prefetch future sequential instructions, so later imem-not-ready cycles are\n  paid in full.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the purely combinational IF-to-ID payload with a tiny two-entry\n  ready/valid fetch skid buffer. The fetch PC should continue issuing\n  sequential requests whenever the buffer is not full, even if ID/EX is held by\n  a dmem stall, load-use bubble, or divide operation. ID consumes from the head\n  of the buffer only when it can accept a new instruction. On EX redirect, the\n  buffer is flushed and fetching restarts at the redirect target, preserving the\n  existing precise RVFI retirement behavior.\n\n  This is structurally different from the failed full IF/ID register: it is a\n  decoupling queue that overlaps independent backend stalls with random imem\n  stalls instead of simply adding a mandatory fetch/decode stage. It also avoids\n  the failed predictor family by keeping branch target decode and tag compares\n  off the live fetch PC path. The expected gain is mostly IPC from hiding some\n  instruction-bus bubbles, with modest timing risk because the queue control is\n  narrow and the existing EX ALU/redirect logic remains unchanged.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add compact fetch-buffer payload metadata if the existing if_id_t fields need an accepted/queued distinction.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Restructure fetch into a two-entry ready/valid instruction buffer with sequential prefetch, dequeue-on-ID-accept, and full flush on redirect.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Separate backend ID-accept stalls from fetch-issue backpressure so the front end can keep filling the buffer while ID/EX is held.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Consume only accepted buffer-head instructions and keep existing decode, legality, and ID/EX bubble semantics for invalid or flushed entries.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the revised fetch/decode ready signals and redirect flush while preserving the nret=1 top-level IO and RVFI retirement contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
