{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"One tempting family would be another branch/predictor tweak, but the logs show those repeatedly create exactly the path this FPGA dislikes. The best structural bet looks like a deeper execute retime that attacks the EX/MEM-to-ALU/address path directly while keeping fetch simple."}}
