{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r9s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-002-r9s1\ntitle: \"Valid-only pipeline bubbles\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  Recent attempts show that adding predictors, fetch buffers, broad predecode,\n  or duplicate execute lanes tends to make the sensitive ID/EX/IF routing worse.\n  The current core still clears or bubbles whole packed pipeline bundles on reset,\n  redirect, load-use, and divider bubbles even though most datapath fields are\n  irrelevant whenever valid is low. Those wide clears and enables add control\n  fanout to the same area that has become the Fmax limiter.\nhypothesis: |\n  Restructure the pipeline registers so the valid bit and side-effecting control\n  fields are the authoritative bubble state, while datapath payload fields are\n  allowed to keep old or newly captured values when valid is zero. On reset,\n  flush, and EX bubble cycles, clear valid plus the control bits that can write a\n  register, issue memory traffic, redirect fetch, or report a trap, but avoid\n  driving zero muxes across rs values, immediates, PCs, instruction words, and\n  RVFI-only payload. Keep the existing MEM/WB hold behavior for dmem stalls so\n  load data remains available for forwarding while retirement valid is cleared.\n\n  This should preserve CoreMark cycles while reducing reset/flush/stall control\n  fanout and packed-struct muxing in the ID/EX, EX/MEM, and MEM/WB registers.\n  It targets the post-champion timing shape without adding predictor state,\n  extra branch latency, or new memory-side arbitration.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Change reset/flush handling to clear only valid and benign control state instead of zeroing the entire ID/EX datapath bundle; keep full holds for real stalls.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Make EX/MEM bubbles clear side-effect control and valid while leaving datapath payload unconstrained, and ensure redirect/memory/writeback control cannot fire from invalid entries.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Gate memory request generation through valid side-effect control, clear only retirement-valid/control on ordinary invalid captures, and preserve the existing dmem-stall forwarding hold semantics.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Pass hazard and forwarding control from side-effect-safe stage state so invalid bubbles cannot create false stalls, redirects, stores, or bypasses.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Keep forwarding based on side-effect-safe producer write enables, with MEM/WB dmem-stall holds still able to forward the retained load result.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
