{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r10s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r10s2\ntitle: \"Narrow registered target predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts show that CoreMark has enough control-flow locality to save cycles, but fetch-side prediction tables, immediate decode, and repair metadata consistently damage the Tang Nano timing path. A nearby result, precomputing branch targets in ID, improved fitness by 3.7% but missed the replacement threshold after adding both pc_plus4 and pc_imm_target payload.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a minimal branch-target predictor that only predicts the PC-relative target for conditional branches and direct JAL, with no direction table and no IF lookup. The ID stage already has the decoded immediate, so it should compute one registered pc_rel_target = pc + imm field and carry only that single 32-bit value into EX. EX will still resolve branch direction with the existing comparator and will still resolve JALR from rs1 + imm, but conditional branch and direct JAL redirect_target/pc_next selection can use the registered target instead of rebuilding pc + imm in the EX redirect cone.\n\n  This is a predictor-category change because it predicts the target early while leaving direction prediction conservative and exact. It avoids the failed BTB/BTFNT/RAS mechanisms, does not add a fetch PC mux input, and trims the wider two-adder ID precompute attempt down to the one value that helps the branch redirect path. The expected win is mostly Fmax, with unchanged CoreMark cycles and low correctness risk.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add one pc_rel_target field to id_ex_t for the registered branch/JAL target prediction, avoiding the wider pc_plus4 plus target payload from the earlier near-miss.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute and latch pc + imm as the predicted PC-relative target for BRANCH and JAL instructions using the existing immediate path.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the registered target for conditional branch and direct JAL redirect_target/pc_next while keeping branch direction, JALR target calculation, traps, and RVFI behavior exact.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add focused coverage for taken/not-taken branches and direct JAL to ensure the registered target preserves architectural pc_wdata and redirect behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
