emVerilog / and %, forcing Gowin to time a full\\nsingle-cycle divider/remainder network even though CoreMark rarely needs\\nthose operations in the measured loop. Removing that arithmetic from the\\none-cycle EX path should raise Fmax far more than the occasional multi-cycle\\ndivide can hurt iterations per cycle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU cases in rtl/alu.sv with a s\n…[142771 of 145843 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:40dbd155defcf673]…\nme\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 113.19, \"delta_pct\": -1.24, \"vs_baseline\": 833.91, \"fmax_mhz\": 50.843, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491817, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2807, \"ff\": 694, \"seeds\": [50.676, 50.843, 50.843], \"perturbations\": [[0, 50.676, 12], [1, 50.843, 14], [2, 50.843, 14]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -14.733, \"arrival_ns\": 25.028, \"logic_cells\": 12, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 12, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T18:44:21.100905Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r10s2 (regression, -1.24%): Even a single registered ID `pc_rel_target` for branch/JAL redirects regressed, implying the added ID adder and 32-bit ID/EX payload cost more timing/routing than removing `pc + imm` from the EX redirect mux cone saves.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
