{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r12s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r12s2\ntitle: \"Tiny hot-loop replay predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts show that ordinary branch prediction is a bad trade\n  for this core: BTBs, static predecode, RAS, and late-verification schemes all\n  paid too much in fetch/control timing for the CoreMark bubbles they saved.\n  The remaining predictor opportunity is to get more value per added mux by\n  using a predictor that also hides the benchmark's random instruction-memory\n  stalls, not just taken-branch redirects.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny hot-loop replay predictor trained only from resolved backward\n  conditional branches. IF keeps a small rolling window of recently accepted\n  fetch PCs and instructions. When EX resolves a taken, aligned backward branch\n  whose target is still in that window and the span fits, freeze that window as\n  a loop trace. On later visits, replay the trace from registered entries,\n  ignore io_imemReady while replaying, and predict the recorded backedge taken\n  by wrapping the replay index to the trace start. Carry only a one-bit\n  predicted-loop-backedge marker with replayed branch instructions so EX can\n  suppress the normal taken redirect; if the branch exits, EX redirects to\n  pc+4, flushes wrong-path replayed instructions, and leaves replay mode.\n\n  This avoids a fetch-side BTB lookup, target adder, return stack, or dynamic\n  counter table. The replay path adds an instruction mux and a small sequencer,\n  but a successful loop trace can remove repeated imem stall bubbles across the\n  whole loop body and remove the recurring backedge redirect bubble. That gives\n  the predictor a larger CoreMark-cycle upside than the earlier branch-only\n  predictors while keeping all architectural verification at EX retirement.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add minimal IF/ID and ID/EX metadata for replayed instructions, including a predicted loop-backedge marker.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Maintain the recent fetch window, enter loop replay from EX-trained backward branches, drive replayed pc/instruction payloads, and hold or repair replay state across stalls and redirects.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Detect eligible aligned backward taken branches, emit loop-train information, suppress redirects for correctly predicted replay backedges, and redirect to pc+4 on loop exits.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire loop-training and replay metadata between IF, ID, and EX while preserving the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_loop_replay.py\n    description: \"Add focused tests for replayed taken loops, loop exit repair, imem stalls during replay, and non-eligible branches falling back to exact EX redirects.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
