{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\"|Predict|predict|branch|JAL|RAS|BTB|BTFNT|loop|replay' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Iterative divider off ALU critical path\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current timed path runs from the forwarding logic through EX and the\\ncombinational ALU, with roughly 150 logic levels. The ALU implements RV32M\\nDIV/REM using SystemVerilog / and %, forcing Gowin to time a full\\nsingle-cycle divider/remainder network even though CoreMark rarely needs\\nthose operations in the measured loop. Removing that arithmetic from the\\none-cycle EX path should raise Fmax far more than the occasional multi-cycle\\ndivide can hurt iterations per cycle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current timed path runs from the forwarding logic through EX and the\\ncombinational ALU, with roughly 150 logic levels. The ALU implements RV32M\\nDIV/REM using SystemVerilog / and %, forcing Gowin to time a full\\nsingle-cycle divider/remainder network even though CoreMark rarely needs\\nthose operations in the measured loop. Removing that arithmetic from the\\none-cycle EX path should raise Fmax far more than the occasional multi-cycle\\ndivide can hurt iterations per cycle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU cases in rtl/alu.sv with a small\\niterative divider/remainder unit that is invoked only when the decoded ALU op\\nis one of the four divide-class RV32M operations. EX holds the pipeline while\\nthe unit is busy, then writes the final quotient or remainder into the normal\\nEX/MEM register with unchanged RVFI contents. Keep MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU on\\nthe existing combinational/DSP path and preserve the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\\nsubstitutions. This should turn the common ADD/compare/address critical path\\nback