{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r14s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r14s2\ntitle: \"Posted-store completion predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The predictor attempts that touched branch target selection, replay fetch, or\n  return prediction consistently lost Fmax because they put table lookup,\n  target muxing, or repair control into the already-sensitive IF/ID/EX routing.\n  A better predictor target is the random dmem stall stream: CoreMark pays full\n  pipeline bubbles when a store sits in MEM and io_dmemReady is low, even though\n  most ordinary RAM stores are not immediately observed by following ALU work.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a one-entry posted-store completion predictor for normal data-memory RAM\n  stores.  When a store reaches MEM while io_dmemReady is low, predict that the\n  store can complete later without affecting younger non-memory instructions:\n  capture its address, replicated write data, byte mask, and RVFI fields in a\n  small store-post register, let the store retire once into MEM/WB, and allow\n  IF/ID/EX to continue instead of freezing the whole pipeline on that dmem stall.\n\n  The predictor is deliberately narrow.  It must not post UART or CoreMark\n  marker MMIO stores, must stall before any younger load/store until the posted\n  store drains or forwards on an exact same-address same-mask hit, and must keep\n  the external dmem write port driven from a single registered arbiter so Gowin\n  still infers the wrapper memory as block RAM.  This avoids the IF PC-select\n  path that doomed branch predictors and aims to recover cycles from the 22%\n  store-stall stream with only registered MEM-side control in the timed core.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add compact posted-store metadata for address, data, mask, RAM/MMIO classification, and exact-drain bookkeeping without changing nret=1.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Implement the one-entry posted-store predictor, retire predicted-posted RAM stores once, drain them through a registered dmem arbiter, and fence MMIO marker/UART stores.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Replace full-pipeline dmem stalls for predicted-posted stores with a store-post hold only when the buffer is full, a younger memory op appears, or an MMIO/marker store must complete exactly.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire posted-store full/drain/conflict signals between MEM and hazard control while preserving the existing imem, dmem, and RVFI port contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_posted_store_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add focused tests for stalled RAM stores retiring once, later drain ordering, same-address load/store serialization, and MMIO marker stores never being posted.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
