{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,200p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r1s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r1s2\ntitle: \"Tiny BTB branch predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current core always fetches fall-through and redirects every taken branch or jump from EX, inserting a bubble on the hot loop branches that CoreMark executes repeatedly. A small predictor should improve iterations/cycle without touching the long ALU/forwarding critical path that currently limits Fmax.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a very small direct-mapped branch target buffer with 2-bit saturating counters, indexed by fetch PC and updated when branches or jumps resolve in EX. The IF stage uses a tagged BTB hit with a taken counter to select the predicted next PC, while ID/EX carries that predicted next PC so EX only redirects and flushes on a mismatch between predicted and resolved next PC. Train unconditional JAL/JALR as taken and train conditional branches by actual outcome; wrong predictions still recover through the existing redirect/flush path. This should remove most recurring taken-branch and repeated call/return bubbles in CoreMark for modest LUT/FF cost and limited Fmax risk.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 12\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add predicted-next-PC metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles so EX can compare prediction against the resolved next PC.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a tiny tagged direct-mapped BTB with 2-bit counters, fetch-side prediction, and EX-side update inputs.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Propagate the fetch prediction metadata into the ID/EX register alongside the instruction and PC.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Resolve the actual next PC, update the predictor for branches and jumps, and assert redirect only when actual and predicted next PC differ.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire predictor update signals between EX and IF while preserving the existing top-level IO contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
