{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r2s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r2s2\ntitle: \"Stateless backward branch predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The previous BTB predictor attempted to recover taken-branch bubbles but paid\n  for tags, counters, target storage, and a fetch-side table lookup on an FPGA\n  timing path that is already sensitive. CoreMark still has hot loop backedges\n  and direct jumps, so there is predictor value available, but it should be\n  pursued with far less state and no associative/tag machinery.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the BTB idea with a stateless fetch predecode predictor: predict\n  conditional branches with negative B-immediates as taken, predict forward\n  conditional branches as not taken, and predict direct JAL targets exactly from\n  the fetched instruction. The IF stage computes a predicted next PC only from\n  the current PC and instruction bits, while ID/EX carries that predicted next\n  PC into EX. EX already computes the resolved next PC; it should flush and\n  redirect only when the static prediction differs from the resolved path.\n  This targets the common CoreMark loop-backedge penalty without LUT-RAM,\n  counters, tags, or a BTB target mux, so the IPC gain should have much lower\n  Fmax risk than the failed tiny-BTB attempt.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid metadata to IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Predecode BRANCH/JAL instructions, compute a stateless BTFNT/JAL predicted next PC, and use it for PC advance when imem data is valid.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Carry the fetch prediction metadata into the ID/EX register with the instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare the resolved next PC with the carried prediction and redirect only on misprediction, preserving existing trap and misalignment behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire any renamed prediction/redirect signals while preserving the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
