{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r3s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r3s2\ntitle: \"One-entry loop backedge predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The previous predictor attempts showed that CoreMark has useful taken-branch\n  locality, but fetch-side BTB lookup or stateless instruction predecode can\n  cost more Fmax than the saved bubbles are worth. A predictor for this core\n  needs to be almost entirely trained from already-resolved EX information and\n  keep immediate assembly, opcode decode, counters, and tag RAM off the live\n  imem-to-PC path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a single-entry loop backedge predictor that remembers the last resolved\n  taken backward conditional branch. IF compares the current PC against the\n  stored branch PC tag and, on a hit, advances to the stored target instead of\n  PC+4. The target is learned in EX from the normal branch_target calculation,\n  so IF does not predecode imem_data or build a target adder. ID/EX carries the\n  predicted next PC and a predicted-taken bit; EX compares the resolved next PC\n  with the prediction and redirects only on mismatch, so loop exits and aliases\n  recover through the existing flush path.\n\n  This targets CoreMark's hot loop backedges with much less timing risk than\n  the failed BTB and BTFNT attempts. It should recover most repeated taken-loop\n  bubbles while adding only a small registered target, a PC tag compare, and an\n  EX-side prediction check. Training only backward conditional branches avoids\n  polluting the entry with calls, returns, and forward error paths.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add predicted-next-PC and predicted-taken metadata to IF/ID and ID/EX bundles so EX can verify predictions precisely.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add the one-entry loop predictor state, PC-tag hit logic, predicted PC advance, and EX-resolve training/clear inputs.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Propagate prediction metadata from the IF/ID payload into the ID/EX register without changing decode legality behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute the resolved next PC for every instruction, redirect on prediction mismatch, and emit backward-branch training or loop-exit clear signals.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire prediction metadata and EX training signals between IF, ID, and EX while preserving the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
