{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r4s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r4s2\ntitle: \"Registered lookahead branch predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts showed that CoreMark can benefit from removing\n  recurring taken-branch bubbles, but same-cycle IF prediction logic has been\n  too expensive. BTB tag/counter lookup, stateless immediate predecode, and a\n  one-entry loop predictor all put compare/add/mux work on the fetch PC path and\n  lost more Fmax than they recovered in IPC. The next predictor attempt should\n  keep predictor lookup off the live PC-select cone while preserving exact\n  misprediction recovery for formal and cosim.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny direct-mapped branch target predictor whose lookup is performed one\n  cycle ahead for the next sequential fetch PC, then registered. When that PC is\n  fetched, IF chooses between pc+4 and the already-registered predicted next PC;\n  the current-cycle PC-select path therefore sees only a small mux, not a tag\n  compare, counter read, immediate generator, or target adder. EX trains the\n  table using the already-computed resolved branch or direct-jump target, while\n  ID/EX carries the predicted next PC so EX can compare it against the resolved\n  architectural next PC and redirect only on mismatch.\n\n  This targets the same hot CoreMark loop and direct-jump bubbles that gave the\n  failed predictors their cycle reductions, but with the expensive predictor\n  lookup retimed away from the fetch critical path. A four-entry table with\n  full PC tags and simple valid/taken state should be enough for the tight\n  loops while keeping LUT and routing cost low. Correctness does not depend on\n  immutable instruction memory because EX still compares the carried predicted\n  next PC with the resolved next PC before suppressing a redirect.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add predicted-next-PC metadata to IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles for exact EX-stage prediction verification.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a tiny direct-mapped lookahead BTB, register lookup results for the next sequential PC, hold them across stalls, and use only the registered prediction in the PC-select mux.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Propagate the registered fetch prediction metadata into ID/EX without changing decode legality or regfile read behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare the resolved architectural next PC with the carried prediction, redirect on mismatch, and emit branch/direct-jump training information.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire predictor metadata and EX training signals between IF, ID, and EX while preserving the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
