on can use a small iterative or DSP-friendly sequencer;\\ndivision/remainder should be iterative, with ALTOPS still handled by the\\nformal-only branch. The expected win is a large Fmax recovery because the\\ncritical forwarding-to-ALU-to-register path no longer traverses combinational\\ndivision and wide multiply logic on \n…[54813 of 57885 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6a1beac6b24f0187]…\nome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 107.36, \"delta_pct\": -6.33, \"vs_baseline\": 785.81, \"fmax_mhz\": 48.075, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4478102, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2947, \"ff\": 707, \"seeds\": [47.765, 48.075, 48.075], \"perturbations\": [[0, 47.765, 22], [1, 48.075, 20], [2, 48.075, 20]], \"lutram\": 16, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_ER_s196\", \"slack_ns\": -15.936, \"arrival_ns\": 26.23, \"logic_cells\": 45, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_rf\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 22, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T17:26:30.318325Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-003-r5s2 (regression, -6.33%): Even a canonical-return-only RAS predictor adds imem_data compare/RAS-top muxing to IF and predicted-return repair plumbing through ID/EX, so CoreMark's return-bubble savings did not offset the fetch/control-path timing cost.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
