{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r6s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r6s2\ntitle: \"Countdown loop backedge predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts proved that CoreMark has enough hot taken\n  backedges to reduce cycles, but every design that put a BTB tag compare,\n  immediate predecode, or return pattern match on the live IF path lost more\n  Fmax than it recovered. The remaining promising predictor angle is to keep\n  the fetch decision extremely small while still predicting the dominant\n  repeated loop branch case.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace PC-tagged branch prediction with a single-entry countdown loop\n  predictor trained only by resolved taken backward conditional branches in\n  EX. When such a branch resolves, record its target and the number of\n  sequential fetches from the target back to the branch PC. During later\n  sequential execution, IF decrements this small counter on accepted fetches;\n  when it reaches zero, IF predicts the next PC as the recorded loop target\n  instead of pc+4.\n\n  This removes the 32-bit fetch-PC tag compare and table lookup that hurt the\n  earlier one-entry loop predictor. The IF critical path should see only a\n  small counter-zero test and one predicted-target mux, while ID/EX still\n  carries a predicted-taken bit and predicted target so EX can verify the\n  resolved architectural next PC, suppress correct redirects, and repair on\n  loop exit or alias. The predictor is intentionally narrow: it targets hot\n  CoreMark backedges, avoids calls/returns/direct jumps, and preserves the\n  existing nret=1 IO and RVFI contract.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add predicted-taken and predicted-target metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles so EX can verify countdown-loop predictions precisely.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add the single-entry loop target, loop length/countdown state, accepted-fetch countdown update, predicted-target PC selection, and EX repair/training inputs.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Propagate the countdown predictor metadata into ID/EX without changing decode legality, immediate generation, or regfile read behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare the resolved next PC against the carried prediction, suppress redirects on correct loop predictions, redirect on mismatch, and emit compact backward-branch training/clear signals.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire predictor metadata and EX training/repair signals between IF, ID, and EX while preserving all top-level core ports.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
