{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20261003-003-r2s2\\\") | .hypothesis.hypothesis, \\\"---changes---\\\", (.changes[] | .file + \\\": \\\" + .description)' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20261003-003-r2s2\\\") | .hypothesis.hypothesis, \\\"---changes---\\\", (.changes[] | .file + \\\": \\\" + .description)' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"Replace the BTB idea with a stateless fetch predecode predictor: predict\nconditional branches with negative B-immediates as taken, predict forward\nconditional branches as not taken, and predict direct JAL targets exactly from\nthe fetched instruction. The IF stage computes a predicted next PC only from\nthe current PC and instruction bits, while ID/EX carries that predicted next\nPC into EX. EX already computes the resolved next PC; it should flush and\nredirect only when the static prediction differs from the resolved path.\nThis targets the common CoreMark loop-backedge penalty without LUT-RAM,\ncounters, tags, or a BTB target mux, so the IPC gain should have much lower\nFmax risk than the failed tiny-BTB attempt.\n\n---changes---\nrtl/core_pkg.sv: Add predicted-next-PC and prediction-valid metadata to IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\nrtl/if_stage.sv: Predecode BRANCH/JAL instructions, compute a stateless BTFNT/JAL predicted next PC, and use it for PC advance when imem data is valid.\nrtl/id_stage.sv: Carry the fetch prediction metadata into the ID/EX register with the instruction.\nrtl/ex_stage.sv: Compare the resolved next PC with the carried prediction and redirect only on misprediction, preserving existing trap and misalignment behavior.\nrtl/core.sv: Wire any renamed prediction/redirect signals while preserving the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20261003-003-r4s2\\\") | .hypothesis.hypothesis, \\\"---changes---\\\", (.changes[] | .file + \\\": \\\" + .description)' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"Add a tiny direct-mapped branch target predictor whose lookup is performed one\ncycle ahead for the next sequential fetch PC, then registered. When that PC is\nfetched, IF chooses between pc+4 and the already-registered predicted next PC;\nthe current-cycle PC-select path therefore sees only a small mux, not a tag\ncompare, counter read, immediate generator, or target adder. EX trains the\ntable using the already-computed resolved branch or direct-jump target, while\nID/EX carries the predicted next PC so EX can compare it against the resolved\narchitectural next PC and redirect only on mismatch.\n\nThis targets the same hot CoreMark loop and direct-jump bubbles that gave the\nfailed predictors their cycle reductions, but with the expensive predictor\nlookup retimed away from the fetch critical path. A four-entry table with\nfull PC tags and simple valid/taken state should be enough for the tight\nloops while keeping LUT and routing cost low. Correctness does not depend on\nimmutable instruction memory because EX still compares the carried predicted\nnext PC with the resolved next PC before suppressing a redirect.\n\n---changes---\nrtl/core_pkg.sv: Add predicted-next-PC metadata to IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles for exact EX-stage prediction verification.\nrtl/if_stage.sv: Add a tiny direct-mapped lookahead BTB, register lookup results for the next sequential PC, hold them across stalls, and use only the registered prediction in the PC-select mux.\nrtl/id_stage.sv: Propagate the registered fetch prediction metadata into ID/EX without changing decode legality or regfile read behavior.\nrtl/ex_stage.sv: Compare the resolved architectural next PC with the carried prediction, redirect on mismatch, and emit branch/direct-jump training information.\nrtl/core.sv: Wire predictor metadata and EX training signals between IF, ID, and EX while preserving the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
