{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r9s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r9s2\ntitle: \"Dynamic late branch verifier\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts that touched IF or decode lost timing through PC\n  target lookup, immediate adders, or prediction metadata. The one predictor\n  direction that kept Fmax roughly intact was late-verified BTFNT, but its\n  static policy lost too many cycles on loop exits and forward-taken branches.\n  A dynamic outcome predictor placed entirely in EX can target the same\n  redirect critical path without adding fetch-side prediction hardware.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny PC-indexed dynamic conditional-branch outcome predictor in\n  ex_stage. The predictor is read using the registered branch PC already in\n  ID/EX, not the live fetch PC, so IF still fetches fall-through and sees no\n  table lookup, tag compare, target adder, or predicted-PC sideband. For a\n  conditional branch in EX, the predictor's taken/not-taken bit drives the\n  same-cycle redirect decision: predicted taken redirects to the normal\n  branch_target, predicted not-taken falls through. The real rs1/rs2 branch\n  comparison still runs in parallel for RVFI pc_next and correctness, but it\n  only updates the predictor and launches a one-cycle repair redirect when\n  the prediction was wrong.\n\n  Compared with the failed static late-verify BTFNT attempt, this keeps the\n  rs comparator off the immediate redirect control path while learning the\n  actual behavior of hot CoreMark branches. Correctly predicted loop\n  backedges behave like today's taken branches, correctly predicted loop\n  exits avoid repeated false-taken repairs, and forward-taken branches become\n  learned after their first miss. The intended gain is Fmax from a simpler\n  EX-to-IF redirect cone with little or no steady-state CoreMark IPC loss.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a tiny dynamic branch-outcome predictor read from the registered EX-stage branch PC, drive conditional redirect from the prediction, update counters from the real comparison, and annul/repair on mispredicts.\"\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add a compact 4-entry or 8-entry saturating-counter predictor module for conditional branch outcomes only, with optional tags kept off the IF path.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add focused tests for correctly predicted taken branches, learned loop exits, forward-taken repair, and wrong-path annulment.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
