{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,200p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Posted-store completion predictor\n\nWhat changed:\n- Added a one-entry posted RAM-store buffer in `mem_stage.sv`.\n- Aligned stores to normal RAM (`addr < 0x00100000`) can retire into MEM/WB when `io_dmemReady` is low and the buffer is empty.\n- The dmem port drains the posted store from registered address/data/mask state before accepting any younger memory operation.\n- Younger non-memory instructions continue while the posted store drains.\n- Younger loads/stores, FENCE/FENCE.I, and EBREAK stall until the posted store is externally accepted.\n- MMIO stores, including UART and CoreMark timing marker addresses, are not posted.\n- `hazard_unit.sv` now distinguishes load stalls, non-postable store stalls, post-buffer conflicts, and postable store completion.\n- Added focused cocotb coverage in `test_posted_store_predictor.py`.\n\nDeviations:\n- I did not implement same-address same-mask load/store forwarding out of the posted buffer. The conservative behavior serializes every younger memory operation until the posted store drains.\n- The dmem port remains a single priority arbiter with registered posted-store source state; current loads/stores still use the existing combinational dmem timing.\n\nConcerns:\n- This should recover cycles only when there is useful non-memory work behind a stalled RAM store. Memory-heavy store/load pairs still serialize.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench` in this worktree does not export `NRET` from `core.yaml`; it builds the harness with the default `NRET=2` and fails against this valid `nret: 1` core. Rerunning with `NRET=1` matches the declared contract and passes.\n\nLocal verification:\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: pass.\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_posted_store_predictor.py`: pass.\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py`: pass.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, 2 ELFs tested.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
